{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404282-how-to-sabotage-disrupt-a-demon-s-cult","id":1404282,"title":"How to sabotage/disrupt a demon's cult?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-23T12:40:05-07:00","id":1404282,"title":"How to sabotage/disrupt a demon's cult?","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> One of the players in my game is the loyal student of a Second Circle Demon. So far we haven't discussed this demon's cult yet but as part of an upcoming story, I want someone to start disrupting this cult to antagonize the demon (which then draws the PC in to go deal with the problem). However, I'm getting stuck after &quot;kill a bunch of worshippers&quot; or &quot;trick the cultists into worshipping someone else&quot;. I was hoping you might have some creative ideas to sabotage a demon's worship?<br /> I'm mostly looking for solutions that don't require a lot of violence and that are more subtle than overt. The antagonist has access to Exalted-level power, so no need to hold back.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:08:05-07:00","id":1404289,"title":"","content":"Destroy holy sites?<br /> Swap sacrifices for forgeries?<br /> Alter the cultists' calendars so they celebrate on the wrong day?<br /> Forge fake holy books so the cultists offer the wrong celebrations.<br /> Convince another god/demon/ghost/anything that wants worship to disrupt the demon to get rid of competition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:23:21-07:00","id":1404293,"title":"","content":"I feel as though this is a question that requires knowing who the demon is, because they run a wide gamut of very diverse types that would probably entail cults with extremely different organisational structures, priorities and rituals that should probably be important to know to give concrete ideas on how to structurally undermine them.<br /> <br /> I mean, assuming that it intends to engage with the cult in a manner other than just gathering informants to find out their membership and meeting locations, the kind of thing that has been done to break up gatherings of underground religious groups for centuries (or even millenia, given the early experiences of Christianity). It's not really necessary to kill, if people are gathered illicitly and somebody in opposition or authority bursts in on them, they're liable to scatter, and doing that enough times to prevent a sense of cohesive community can mean that people gradually stop trying, especially if the main organising and charismatic figures are unable to operate.<br /> <br /> Mind, again thinking about things like early Christianity or, say, underground English Catholicism, people in those situations can also often employ things like signs and signals that are impenetrable to outsiders and provide a sense of solidarity to fellows even if they're prevented from gathering (it can help a group to just receive frequent reminders that they're not alone in things), and would be kind of difficult to catch somebody doing without a level of surveillance that's difficult to apply in much of the game's world and can have a level of plausible deniability even if they are.<br /> <br /> ...I'm sorry, I didn't fully read your post and was not quite coming at this from the correct angle. Yeah if the protagonists have solidarity with the underground group, then I'd go with the antagonists employing those means of intelligence gathering, targeting leading community figures (and severe measures employed against those known to have harboured them) and creating a general environment of paranoia around the use of secret signs. If an opposing Exalt or similar can figure out the innocuous phrase intended to identify somebody as a member of the group, teach it to their agents, and then have those people make a very public example of those whom they catch stating it (with little reservation for pleas that it was completely normal), then the group can have a hard time effectively communicating with one another.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that in circumstances like this, it can be difficult to effectively gather in secrecy; pre-modern cities tend to be fairly confined and people know one another's business, so it's often not hard to take notice that a large group is gathering frequently and trying to avoid notice, especially if an active watch can be put out for them; there's a reason Christians had to gather in catacombs, spaces that were reasonably large, out of the way and carried taboos against being watched too closely. Some kind of cover story can help, but that still requires that the antagonising element can be expected to believe it, or care much about the possibility of persecuting innocent people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T02:50:54-07:00","id":1404372,"title":"","content":"Mind, I'm thinking about historical instances of persecution of underground groups and... it definitely makes their lives more miserable and weakens their capacity to accumulate social, but it hardly ever seems to effectively eliminate them, does it? People can endure under such conditions for a pretty long time.<br /> <br /> If the antagonist has the proper kind of cunning, they'll run a campaign on two fronts. The mailed fist is groping about to do those things I was talking about to suss out communications and hiding places and break them apart, while the other hand offers a slightly browned olive branch; figure out what it is that has driven so many people into the arms of this group and try to make some concessions that address them just enough (and on the terms of the authority) to make people find the compromise preferable to the life of dedicated persecution. It won't satisfy all, but if the die hards are isolated they can ultimately drift into obscurity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T05:00:17-07:00","id":1404381,"title":"","content":"Infiltrate a gathering and then start spreading a disease amongst them, like leprosy, which ruins their livelihoods and basically turns them into pariahs. Your player has to start figuring out a cure, or have a cult that is considered to be filthy and unholy. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, your Antagonist has Exalted level powers. That means that it probably has mind control, whether or not its from socialising or from sorcery. Grab one or two people, turn them into sleeper agents, and then have them randomly stab when they're in there for gatherings. Sooner or later no one would come, too mistrustful and too afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}